.TH COMPUTER-MCP-BACKEND 1 "September 2026" "computer-mcp-backend 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
computer-mcp-backend \- Linux VM guest MCP runtime
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B node dist/index.js
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the MCP server inside a Linux VM. It performs X11 desktop control, shell/filesystem operations, and Selenium browser automation. The host-side SSH proxy is maintained separately in Computer-MCP.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Use Node.js 20 or newer, a logged-in X11 session, Firefox, ffmpeg, xdotool, xclip, xrandr, Git, curl, and build tools. Wayland is detected but direct GUI capture and input are not implemented.
.SH INSTALLATION
On Debian or Ubuntu:
.EX
sudo apt update
sudo apt install ffmpeg xdotool xclip x11-xserver-utils git curl build-essential nodejs npm firefox-esr
npm ci
npm run build
.EE
The setup-vm.sh helper installs the exact APT packages, performs build/tests/lint, and never creates or changes a VM. Run the helper as the graphical user, not with sudo for the whole script. If the checkout is root-owned, it uses sudo chown -R on that project directory so the user can create node_modules and dist. Do not use sudo npm. The test-vm.sh validator is non-destructive.
.SH PACKAGES
The exact APT packages are ffmpeg, xdotool, xclip, x11-xserver-utils, git, curl, build-essential, firefox-esr, nodejs, and npm. Equivalent manual commands are documented in README.md for Fedora/RHEL-like, Arch/Manjaro, openSUSE, and Alpine.
.SH MCP TOOLS
The runtime exposes desktop screenshot, mouse, keyboard, clipboard, monitor, shell/filesystem, and Selenium tools over MCP stdio. Use browser_start for visible or headless Selenium and computer_screenshot for the whole X11 desktop.
.SH MCPO
.EX
mcpo --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8084 -- node /opt/computer-mcp-backend/dist/index.js
.EE
MCPO is installed separately. The host-side Computer-MCP repository can forward MCP stdio to this command over SSH.
.SH VALIDATION
.EX
./scripts/test-vm.sh
npm run build
npm test
npm run lint
.EE
The validator checks the X11 display, commands, browser, monitors, FFmpeg capture, build, tests, and MCP discovery without changing input or clipboard state.
.SH SECURITY
The VM is the execution boundary. Do not mount host filesystems, expose the host Docker socket, copy host credentials or browser profiles, or disable SSH host-key verification. No host command, host filesystem, hypervisor, or VM escape facility is implemented.
.SH LIMITATIONS
The GUI path targets X11. Selenium driver/browser resolution depends on the installed browser, Selenium Manager, and VM network. The runtime must execute on Linux.
